{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetVolumeRigidity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetVolumeRigidity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Instance"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetVolumeRigidity.eq_blochD_of_value_at_I","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetVolumeRigidity.eq_blochD_of_value_at_I","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetVolumeRigidity.lean#L46-L52","doc":"**The calibrated form.** If moreover `V(i) = D(i)` (the regular ideal octahedron's\nquarter, i.e. the right-angled shape), then `V = D` on `ℂ ∖ {0,1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetVolumeRigidity.eq_div_mul_blochD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetVolumeRigidity.eq_div_mul_blochD","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetVolumeRigidity.lean#L34-L44","doc":"**Rigidity for a volume-type function.** Under continuity, the Bloch–Wigner symmetries and\nthe five-term relation, `V` is the multiple of `D` fixed by its value at `i`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}